<title>SPAIN: Spain mining industry to shrink in next 5 years.</title>
<headline>Spain mining industry to shrink in next 5 years.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's mining industry, facing a declining demand, is expected to shrink in the next five years, with state aid falling 35 percent and with three of ten jobs being cut, according to a draft agreement between trade unions and Industry Ministry, local media reported.</p>
<p>The plan forecasts a reduction of between 7,000 and 25,000 jobs in the industry, while state aids are expected to be cut to 107 billion pesetas in 2005 from the current 142 bln pta.</p>
<p>At the same time coal consumption is expected to fall to around 13 tonnes in 2005 from the current 18 tonns.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
